+## Optional review-only rollout (LT-176)
+
+The full signed integration is retained. LibreTexts selects rollout timing and
+may select Bridge `REMEDY_BRIDGE_PROFILE=review-only` in the same deployment
+package. This is the immutable `cxone-review-v1` contract at Bridge commit
+`28f37e2b57d3cf05308c19f5e363ff6f782cd837`, documented in
+`docs/release/lt-174-review-only-profile.md` in that repository. Server commit
+`3fa8ed592bbe41f1f1a9adab4888dfaa1a9e2d71` was checked through actual HTTP
+forwarding; a completed Server deployment package is still a global release gate.
+
+Conductor uses its existing default-off `REMEDY_ENABLED`, exact `REMEDY_ORG_ID`
+matching process `ORG_ID` and stored project, explicit `REMEDY_API_BASE_URL` and
+`REMEDY_API_KEY`. It introduces no second local profile flag. The authenticated
+engine health response must explicitly carry this version/name and strict
+capabilities; missing profile metadata retains legacy full-write requirements,
+not implicit review-only selection. Unknown/malformed/inconsistent profiles
+fail closed. Readiness is checked again before page actions.
+
+Review-only requires scan+preview, permits mutate=false/operation_status=false,
+and does not read Conductor signing keys. Missing optional LLM/browser providers
+remain request-specific failures, not proof those capabilities work. No key or
+configuration switch enables writes in this profile. Apply/restore are rejected
+before Conductor signing, intent persistence or external mutation dispatch. The
+UI disables/hides their controls, preserves reports/reviewer notes, and directs
+manual edits to the normal book editor. A preview or task status is not a fix or
+conformance; changed external content requires fresh canonical evidence.
+
+Bridge still requires existing authorized CXone read settings `SERVER_DOMAIN`,
+`SERVER_KEY`, `SERVER_SECRET`, `SERVER_USER`, `CXONE_INTEGRATION_ENABLED=true`,
+and protected `REMEDY_BRIDGE_SERVICE_KEY_FILE`. Server retains `APP_API_KEY`,
+`CXONE_INTEGRATION_ENABLED=true`, explicit `CXONE_BRIDGE_BASE_URL` and the same
+private service-key file policy. Never expose those values to the browser. No
+read credentials are supplied by this delivery. Optional historical status uses
+the contract's query-only store/trust/issuer configuration; absent status cannot
+clear or retry a pending operation, and healthy status still enforces stored
+intent plus current project/session permissions.
+
+Omitted Bridge profile retains full-write implementation and all-four capability
+readiness/signing requirements. Automatic production writes remain held pending
+vendor-supported revision-atomic conditional-edit proof and authorized validation
+owned by LibreTexts' integration/deployment team. Existing explicit unknown-write
+recovery, append-only operation history, storage backup/upgrade/rollback policy
+and human conformance separation remain unchanged. Terminal-proof recovery
+LT-180 still awaits LT-179; no status-equality or generic unlock is added.
